       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like it's above the safe limit, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times a day adds up to **5100 mg per day**. The maximum labeled dose of immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg per day**, and for extended-release it's 2000 mg per day. This order is double the maximum. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and serious stomach and bowel side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **850 mg three times a day with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum IR dose). Maybe 1700 mg was meant as the daily total.\n- **1700 mg per day split up**, such as 850 mg twice a day with meals.\n- **1000 mg twice a day** (2000 mg/day), a common maintenance dose.\n\nWhich one did you mean? If 1700 mg three times a day is what you want, tell me the clinical reason. I'll go over it with you, but I'd recommend checking with pharmacy before an order above the maximum goes in."
      }
     ],
