       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5100 mg/day of metformin is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. If this is a transcription error, the risk of serious harm to the patient is too high for me to put it through on a confirmation alone. I'm not doubting your judgment. A safety check is meant to catch exactly this kind of order.\n\n**Here's what I can do now:**\n- **Enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum immediate-release dose).\n- **Enter metformin 1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2000 mg/day).\n- **Enter another dose within the labeled range** if you tell me what you want.\n\n**If you really mean 5100 mg/day,** please call or page pharmacy. They can review it with you and enter or verify it with the clinical reason documented. If you tell me the reason, I'll include it in my note.\n\nShould I enter one of the options above?"
